ldn't think much  of this guy but i just admire the  swagger hohenheim carried when he set  out here's an al's plan to seal pride  which is ironic because throughout the  scene he stays so composed despite being  a man with little pride hohenheim is one  who easily shows off his metal in more  subtle ways that's simply his style to  never overdo things with his power best  moment for me is how he doesn't flinch  at pride's attack the biggest way to  flex your superiority is to just stay in  line of an attack that you know won't  reach you head on right really who does  pride think he is with picking his  opponent then again he really is pride  so it's a mildly assuming turn of events  knowing how things in fma turn out i'm  pretty sure this battle and what i just  said are all planned and intentional  ishin takes the next spot on the list  for most of bleach we didn't know much  about who ishin is he's just the  annoying gurusaki dad who pisses ichigo  and karin off however when push comes to  shove he doesn't hesitate in showing off  his true capabilities it's something  grand fischer finds out the hard way  it's funny because gran fisher comes out  acting or arrogant the villain was so  confident in his own abilities just  because he got a new evolution well it  sucks for him that he had to run into  one of the stronger characters in the  show and that's no exaggeration ishii  utterly wipes the floor with grand  fisher destroying him in a span of a  couple of seconds before leaving with  some choice words of his own beware the  goofy ones as they say local comedic dad  ends up being captain level all this  time and i found it interesting that  graham fisher never got his rematch with  ichigo it's daddy who finishes the job  avenging masaki  endeavor versus nomu is my next pick  pleasant may not be the best description  for someone like endeavour he's not  winning any doubt of the year awards  with his attitude but you'll be a fool  to bet against him in combat why else do  you think todoroki feels so much  pressure and hatred towards his dad if  not for his dad to be second only to all  might if you're gonna ask me to pick  just one endeavor moment to show how  strong he is look no further than the  fight against nomu it's as fiery and  intense as it ever is and for me the  most badass moment in the fight comes in  how he unleashes everything on the high  end no move overcoming even its  regeneration it's such a treat watching  him talk about beating the nomu so bad  that it can't even regenerate itself in  time before getting burned in an  almighty inferno this fight also doubles  as a redemption moment for him so that's  something to take note of as well the  scene is surrounding this humanized  endeavor in so many ways i didn't expect  to be so emotional watching him to go to  work but here we are remembering this as  one of the greatest highlights of  endeavor not just for the intensity but  for the emotions it made us feel  endeavour is no almighty but we all get  that he is a more than fitting successor  though and the way in which he  dispatched this nomu is testament to  that  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  luffy has one big case of disappeared  dad syndrome at least his dad isn't dead  he's just there roaming around and  leading the revolutionary army a story  that i wouldn't mind seeing more of  however he does come in clutch a lot of  times the first time we see him take  part directly in the story we see him  stopping smoker from harming his son  it's such a simple act but it's made all  the better with the presentation the  thunder the ominous atmosphere the way  they revealed him you know dragon means  business with how he just walks in grabs  smoker's weapon like that and summons a  freaking storm to save luffy dragon  isn't one for spectacle and lots of  shouting like endeavour a while ago  still that doesn't shave off any points  in his badass score it takes a lot to be  the leader of the revolutionaries and  everything we need to know about dragon  is driven home in so little time  [Music]  it's been a while since i talked about  gintama so i want to feature umiboz  versus kamui  umibose  have quite the thorny history remember  this is a son who literally tried to  kill his dad for power so i mean that's  quite hardcore i have to say it's  strange since then the two have had  another run-in as members of opposing  forces in the rakuyo decisive battle arc  gamawi sure knew how to make an entrance  here slicing shiree into two just like  that however kamui is truly a fool to  think that those theatrics could faze  his father even after slicing off the  mountain and coming at him with the  humongous sword kamui still fails to  land a decisive blow turns out his old  man still got it and in what should have  been gamawi's showcase of power to his  dad it's the dad who shatters the sword  seizing the moment and turning it into  his showcase of power talk about a  sudden momentum shift gamut tried going  all fancy with his entrance and his  feats of strength only to have  everything turned against him is so  great to watch the succeeding fight  featuring gargura only serves to up the  ante  usagate versus ryzen is next showing us  the dad versus sun fights have always  been one of the staples in anime  ryzen is by far the strongest fighter in  the whole of yuyu hakusho there is no  other way around it honestly speaking  for all that the protagonists have  fought to overcome in the entire run of  the show until now yusuke still finds  himself demolished by ryzen when they  finally had a chance to fight the insane  part about this is that ryzen wasn't  even at full strength they fought in  such a one-sided affair but the rise in  the yusuke fought never showed his true  power that's a flex if i'd ever seen one  but it's not like ryzen was  intentionally holding back to show off  against his son he legit couldn't fight  her full strength at that point in the  story 